---
// src/pages/terms.astro — Terms of Service. Static content page, zero JS.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms that govern use of Root My Android: accounts, subscriptions, payments, acceptable use, and warranty disclaimers."
>
  <div class="container prose px-5 py-12">
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="faint"><em>Last updated: November 5, 2026</em></p>

    <p>
      These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your use of Root My Android ("the Service", "we",
      "us"), including the rootmyandroid.com website, the Root My Android API, and the Rootz and
      Guardian Angel Android applications. By using the Service you agree to these Terms.
    </p>

    <h2>1. What the Service is</h2>
    <p>
      The Service provides software tools, device analysis, and educational information for
      Android devices: scanning a device you connect, assessing its backup coverage, bootloader
      and root status, producing rooting / upgrade plans, encrypted backup storage, and related
      device-management features. Certain features are provided free of charge; advanced
      ("PRO") features are offered as prepaid subscription plans (see
      <a href="/pricing">Pricing</a>).
    </p>

    <h2>2. Accounts</h2>
    <p>
      Accounts are identified by a randomly generated 16-digit account number. We do not require
      or store an email address, password, name, or any other personal identifier.
      <strong>You are solely responsible for saving your account number.</strong> Because we hold
      no recovery information, a lost account number cannot be recovered and any subscription
      time or synced data attached to it becomes permanently inaccessible. Do not share your account
      number; anyone holding it can use the account.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each account can be linked to up to <strong>5 devices</strong> at a time. Device changes
      may be rate-limited to prevent sharing abuse.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Subscriptions and prepaid time</h2>
    <p>
      Paid plans (see <a href="/pricing">Pricing</a>) are prepaid subscriptions: you top up your
      account with a block of subscription time — 30 days for Guardian Angel plans, 365 days for
      Rootz Pro — and the plan stays active until that time runs out. There is no automatic
      renewal and no stored payment method; extending a plan is always a new, explicit purchase.
      Guardian Angel offers two plans (Lite and Pro) and you may top up either at any time.
      Subscription time:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>is not money, cryptocurrency, or a security, and has no value outside the Service;</li>
      <li>is not redeemable, exchangeable, or refundable for cash or cryptocurrency;</li>
      <li>is tied to the account number it was purchased for and is not transferable;</li>
      <li>elapses with calendar time, whether or not the plan's features are used.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>4. Payments</h2>
    <p>
      Payments are accepted in cryptocurrency. Cryptocurrency payments receive a 15% discount
      off listed USD prices — crypto costs us less in fees and administration, and we pass that
      back. Card / Apple Pay purchases, when offered, are
      processed by a third-party on-ramp that converts your payment to cryptocurrency on our
      behalf; that provider's own terms and identity checks apply to those transactions. We never
      see or store your card number. Cryptocurrency payments are irreversible by design; see our
      <a href="/refunds">Refund Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>You agree to use the Service only on devices that:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>you own, or</li>
      <li>you are explicitly authorized by the owner to manage or modify — including, for the
        Guardian Angel application, devices used by your minor children under your legal
        guardianship.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      You may not use the Service to access, modify, or extract data from devices without the
      owner's authorization, to violate any law, or to interfere with the Service's operation.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Rooting, unlocking, and modification risk</h2>
    <p>
      Rooting, unlocking a bootloader, or installing aftermarket firmware on a device
      <strong>may void the manufacturer's warranty, erase the device, trigger security
      protections (e.g. SafetyNet / Play Integrity), or render the device unusable
      ("bricked")</strong>. Any plan, guide, or tool the Service provides is offered as
      information and tooling only; the decision and the act of modifying a device — and all
      consequences of that act — are entirely yours.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Backups, sync, and encryption</h2>
    <p>
      Backup and device-sync features encrypt data on your device before upload; the encryption
      key is held by you and never by us. <strong>We cannot decrypt your backups or synced data
      and cannot recover a lost key.</strong> Losing your key means losing your backups.
    </p>

    <h2>8. No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      THE SERVICE IS PROVIDED "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE" WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
      IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A
      PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT. WE DO NOT WARRANT THAT ANY ROOT METHOD, ROM, OR
      GUIDE WILL WORK ON ANY PARTICULAR DEVICE, OR THAT THE SERVICE WILL BE UNINTERRUPTED OR
      ERROR-FREE.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, IN NO EVENT SHALL WE BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT,
      INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, OR ANY LOSS OF DATA, DEVICE
      FUNCTIONALITY, OR PROFITS, ARISING FROM YOUR USE OF THE SERVICE. OUR TOTAL AGGREGATE
      LIABILITY FOR ANY CLAIM RELATING TO THE SERVICE SHALL NOT EXCEED THE AMOUNT YOU PAID US IN
      THE 30 DAYS PRECEDING THE CLAIM.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Termination</h2>
    <p>
      We may suspend or refuse service to any account used in violation of these Terms, including
      payment abuse. Because accounts are anonymous, enforcement is by account number.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these Terms from time to time. The current version is always published at
      <a href="/terms">rootmyandroid.com/terms</a> with its revision date. Continued use after a
      change constitutes acceptance.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these Terms:
      <a href="mailto:support@rootmyandroid.com">support@rootmyandroid.com</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
